review_comments.body:
**Breaking:** Gating capture only inside `ScreenshotCapturer` leaves `ChangeDetector` running while the app is inactive or paused, which burns its forced-tick retry budget and strands static screens unrecorded after returning to `AppLifecycleState.resumed`.

- **Contract & evidence:** `posthog_flutter`'s replay pipeline guarantees static screens get an initial or post-reset frame via `ChangeDetector.start()` (`posthog_flutter/lib/src/replay/change_detector.dart:54-63`) and `PostHogWidgetState._sampleRetryTicks = 3` (`posthog_flutter/lib/src/posthog_widget.dart:89-120`). Because `ChangeDetector.start()` keeps running its periodic timer (`change_detector.dart:64-70`) and `_scheduleFrameCallback()` unconditionally calls `scheduleFrame()` / `addPostFrameCallback()` (`change_detector.dart:109-122`), every tick while `inactive` decrements `_forcedTicksLeft` and drops the capture at `screenshot_capturer.dart:657-659`. Likewise, mounting `PostHogWidget` while `inactive` spends the single synchronous `requestImmediateSample()` (where `_forcedTicksLeft == 0`). When the app returns to `resumed` on a static screen, nothing forces a frame, so `sendMetaEvent` and `sendFullSnapshot` never fire. While `paused`, the periodic timer also keeps calling `scheduleFrame()` (when `_forcedTicksLeft > 0` or `hasCapturedPlatformViews == true`) and queueing `addPostFrameCallback` closures every `throttleDelay` with no frames draining them.
- **Minimal realistic trigger:** User has `PostHogWidget` mounted with `sessionReplay = true`; `Posthog().reset()` (or `PostHogWidget` mount / `optIn()` / occlusion end) occurs while the app is `inactive` (e.g., permission dialog, notification shade, Control Center, or app switcher) for >= 3s at the default 1s `throttleDelay`; user returns to `resumed` on a static screen.
- **Actual vs expected (verified on merge base `78c5a5d0` vs head `959f5a1e`):**
  - `reset()` during `inactive` → `resumed`: **PASS** on base (`metaIdx=2, fullIdx=3`), **FAIL** on head (`metaIdx=-1, fullIdx=-1`).
  - Mount during `inactive` → `resumed`: **PASS** on base (`fullCount=1`), **FAIL** on head (`fullCount=0`).
  - `ChangeDetector` scheduling frames while `inactive`: **FAIL** on both base and head (`hasScheduledFrame == true` on tick 0 while `inactive`).
- **SDK user / analytics impact:** Missing replay opening frames (blank/unplayable sessions) after ordinary `inactive -> resumed` transitions on static screens on both Android and iOS, plus continued background frame scheduling (directly conflicting with issue #741 item 1) and unbounded `addPostFrameCallback` queueing while paused.
- **Recommendation:** Consider mixing `WidgetsBindingObserver` into `PostHogWidgetState` (`posthog_flutter/lib/src/posthog_widget.dart`) to pause `_changeDetector?.stop()` (which already preserves `_forcedTicksLeft`, per `change_detector.dart:88-89`) and cancel in-flight screenshot captures when leaving `resumed`, and call `_changeDetector?.start()` upon returning to `resumed` (also deferring the initial `start()` in `initState()` if `lifecycleState` is already non-null and non-`resumed`). Note that skipping `ChangeDetector` ticks alone would still fail the mount-while-inactive case because `start()` calls `requestImmediateSample()` once synchronously with `_forcedTicksLeft == 0`. Keep `_buildOcclusionPlaceholder()` working when Android native occlusion fires while the host activity is stopped.
- **Regression tests:**
```dart
testWidgets(
    'reset during inactive period still captures static screen after resuming',
    (tester) async {
  await mount(tester, 1.0);
  calls.clear();

  tester.binding.handleAppLifecycleStateChanged(AppLifecycleState.inactive);
  try {
    sessionId = 'session-b';
    await Posthog().reset();
    for (var i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
      await tester.pump(const Duration(seconds: 1));
      await settleCapture(tester, rounds: 4);
    }
  } finally {
    tester.binding.handleAppLifecycleStateChanged(AppLifecycleState.resumed);
  }

  for (var i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
    await tester.pump(const Duration(seconds: 1));
    await settleCapture(tester, rounds: 4);
  }

  final meta = calls.indexWhere((call) => call.method == 'sendMetaEvent');
  final full = calls.indexWhere((call) => call.method == 'sendFullSnapshot');
  expect(meta, greaterThanOrEqualTo(0));
  expect(full, greaterThan(meta));
  await unmount(tester);
}, variant: TargetPlatformVariant.only(TargetPlatform.android));

testWidgets(
    'mounting while inactive captures static screen once app resumes',
    (tester) async {
  tester.binding.handleAppLifecycleStateChanged(AppLifecycleState.inactive);
  try {
    await mount(tester, 1.0, waitForSnapshot: false);
    await tester.pump(const Duration(seconds: 2));
    await settleCapture(tester, rounds: 4);
  } finally {
    tester.binding.handleAppLifecycleStateChanged(AppLifecycleState.resumed);
  }

  for (var i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
    await tester.pump(const Duration(seconds: 1));
    await settleCapture(tester, rounds: 4);
  }

  expect(calls.where((call) => call.method == 'sendFullSnapshot'), isNotEmpty);
  await unmount(tester);
}, variant: TargetPlatformVariant.only(TargetPlatform.android));
```

**Concern:** `_captureScreenshot()` stops re-checking `_canCaptureInCurrentLifecycle` after `endOfFrame` (line 718), so an in-flight capture that becomes inactive during `renderObject.toImage()`, `toByteData()`, or `captureNativeScreenshots()` still runs subsequent GPU rasterization (`currentPicture.toImage()`), GPU readbacks (`toByteData()`), and Android `PixelCopy` calls while inactive.

- **Contract & evidence:** Every non-duplicate screenshot performs a second GPU rasterization (`currentPicture.toImage(imageWidth, imageHeight)` at line 892) and two GPU readbacks (`_getImageBytes` / `toByteData` at lines 768 and 912), plus optional native `PixelCopy` (`captureNativeScreenshots` at line 867, up to a 5s timeout) and `ui.decodeImageFromPixels` (line 877). All post-await checks after line 718 — lines 743, 772, 868, 895, and 913 — only check `_cancelled` (and the `_compositeRevealedView` loop at lines 874–879 has no abort check before line 892). For comparison, `posthog-ios` (`PostHogReplayIntegration.swift:2513-2519`) re-checks `!isInBackground` after its async hop right before GPU encoding (`frame.encode()`).
- **Minimal realistic trigger:** User switches apps or dismisses the foreground activity while an in-flight capture is awaiting `renderObject.toImage()` (line 740), `_getImageBytes(rawRgba)` (line 768), or `captureNativeScreenshots()` (line 867).
- **Actual vs expected (verified on merge base `78c5a5d0` and head `959f5a1e`):** When `AppLifecycleState.inactive` arrives inside `captureNativeScreenshots()`, `captureScreenshot()` continues through `currentPicture.toImage()` (line 892) and `_getImageBytes` (line 912) and returns a non-null `ImageInfo` instead of aborting with `null`.
- **SDK user / analytics impact:** Leaves a realistic mid-capture window open for the same Android Impeller GPU command-encoding crash (#741) or wasted background GPU/surface work when the app leaves the foreground mid-capture.
- **Recommendation:** Consider using a shared `_shouldAbortCapture => _cancelled || !_canCaptureInCurrentLifecycle` check at every async resumption point in `_captureScreenshot()` (lines 718, 743, 772, 868, after the `_compositeRevealedView` loop before line 892, 895, and 913), ensuring intermediate `ui.Image` / `PictureRecorder` / `Picture` handles are disposed on early return. Keep `_buildOcclusionPlaceholder()` (lines 582–646) ungated by lifecycle state, since Android's native occlusion detector intentionally triggers it while the host Flutter activity is stopped (`paused`).
- **Regression test:**
```dart
class _FakePlatformViewController extends PlatformViewController {
  @override
  int get viewId => 1;

  @override
  Future<void> clearFocus() async {}

  @override
  Future<void> dispatchPointerEvent(PointerEvent event) async {}

  @override
  Future<void> dispose() async {}
}

testWidgets(
    'capture aborts before Picture.toImage when app becomes inactive mid-capture',
    (tester) async {
  var nativeCaptureRequested = false;
  final config = PostHogConfig('test_project_token')
    ..sessionReplay = true
    ..sessionReplayConfig.maskAllTexts = false
    ..sessionReplayConfig.maskAllImages = false
    ..sessionReplayConfig.maskAllPlatformViews = false;
  await Posthog().setup(config);

  messenger.setMockMethodCallHandler(channel, (call) async {
    calls.add(call);
    if (call.method == 'getSessionReplayState') {
      return {'isActive': true, 'sessionId': sessionId, 'secure': false};
    }
    if (call.method == 'captureNativeScreenshots') {
      nativeCaptureRequested = true;
      tester.binding.handleAppLifecycleStateChanged(AppLifecycleState.inactive);
      return <Uint8List?>[null];
    }
    return null;
  });

  await tester.pumpWidget(
    Align(
      alignment: Alignment.topLeft,
      child: SizedBox(
        width: 101,
        height: 99,
        child: PostHogWidget(
          child: Stack(
            textDirection: TextDirection.ltr,
            fit: StackFit.expand,
            children: [
              const ColoredBox(color: Color(0xFF00FF00)),
              Positioned(
                left: 10,
                top: 10,
                width: 40,
                height: 40,
                child: PlatformViewSurface(
                  controller: _FakePlatformViewController(),
                  gestureRecognizers: const {},
                  hitTestBehavior: PlatformViewHitTestBehavior.opaque,
                ),
              ),
            ],
          ),
        ),
      ),
    ),
  );
  await tester.pump();

  final capturer = ScreenshotCapturer(config);
  var completed = false;
  final capture = capturer.captureScreenshot().whenComplete(() {
    completed = true;
  });

  try {
    await settleUntil(tester, () => completed);
    expect(completed, isTrue);
    expect(nativeCaptureRequested, isTrue);
    expect(await capture, isNull);
  } finally {
    tester.binding.handleAppLifecycleStateChanged(AppLifecycleState.resumed);
  }
  await unmount(tester);
}, variant: TargetPlatformVariant.only(TargetPlatform.android));
```

**Concern:** The new lifecycle tests leave one of the three added guards (`screenshot_capturer.dart:665`), all non-`inactive` background states (`paused`, `hidden`, `detached`), and Test 2's guard-path assertion uncovered.

- **Contract & evidence:** `ScreenshotCapturer` adds three guard points (lines 657, 665, and 718) intended to skip capture for every non-`resumed` `AppLifecycleState` on both Android and iOS (`posthog_flutter/lib/src/replay/screenshot/screenshot_capturer.dart:648-667,718-721`). In `posthog_flutter/test/replay_screenshot_capture_test.dart:107-159`:
  1. Neither test transitions lifecycle state while `getSessionReplayState()` is in flight, leaving line 665 untested.
  2. Both tests only use `AppLifecycleState.inactive` (on Android only), so a regression narrowing the predicate to `!= AppLifecycleState.inactive` — leaving Android's `onStop` state (`paused`), `hidden`, and `detached` unguarded — would still pass.
  3. Test 2 (`capture drops the frame when the app becomes inactive`) does reach `endOfFrame` today (verified by tracing `getSessionReplayState` before the post-frame callback), but does not assert that `getSessionReplayState` was actually called, so a scheduling change that exits at line 657 would silently drop coverage of line 718.
- **Minimal realistic trigger / verification:** Verified via a regression test flipping to `AppLifecycleState.paused` while `getSessionReplayState` is pending (fails on merge base `78c5a5d0` and passes on head `959f5a1e`).
- **SDK user / analytics impact:** Regressions in the `getSessionReplayState` post-await check, `paused`/`hidden`/`detached` background states, or `endOfFrame` path would go undetected in CI.
- **Recommendation:** Consider adding a test for the post-`getSessionReplayState` guard (line 665), parameterizing Test 1 over `AppLifecycleState.inactive`, `paused`, `hidden`, and `detached` (covering iOS as well as Android), and asserting in Test 2 that `getSessionReplayState` was called once before the capture dropped:
```dart
testWidgets('capture drops when app becomes paused during getSessionReplayState',
    (tester) async {
  final config = await mount(tester, 1.0);
  messenger.setMockMethodCallHandler(channel, (call) async {
    calls.add(call);
    if (call.method == 'getSessionReplayState') {
      tester.binding.handleAppLifecycleStateChanged(AppLifecycleState.paused);
      return {'isActive': true, 'sessionId': sessionId, 'secure': false};
    }
    return null;
  });

  final capturer = ScreenshotCapturer(config);
  var completed = false;
  final capture = capturer.captureScreenshot().whenComplete(() {
    completed = true;
  });
  try {
    await settleUntil(tester, () => completed);
    expect(completed, isTrue);
    expect(await capture, isNull);
  } finally {
    tester.binding.handleAppLifecycleStateChanged(AppLifecycleState.resumed);
  }
  await unmount(tester);
});
```
